# Implementation Plan - 100% Backend Integration Refactings

This plan outlines the technical steps to achieve 100% production-ready backend integration for the **Sport Turfs** platform by centralizing API URLs, standardizing ID schemas across frontend/backend, and enforcing atomic 5-minute slot hold locks in MySQL/Redis.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Technical Decisions for Review:**
> 1. **Centralized API Client**: All raw `fetch('http://localhost:5005/...')` calls across 14+ frontend components will be migrated to use standard helper methods from `src/services/api.js` configured with `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`.
> 2. **ID Normalization Strategy**: Both numeric IDs (e.g. `16`, `1`) and string IDs (e.g. `br_001`, `turf_16`) will be accepted and parsed dynamically in backend controllers via an `normalizeId` utility.
> 3. **Atomic Slot Lock**: During Step 3 checkout, a 5-minute atomic database hold (`status = 'HELD'`, `expires_at = NOW() + INTERVAL 5 MINUTE`) will be written to MySQL with a unique `holdId` to guarantee two users cannot lock or purchase the same slot concurrently.

